Package: imputefinder
Title: Condition-Aware Missingness Classification for Proteomics
Version: 0.99.8
Authors@R:
    person("Emir", "Turkes", email = "emir.turkes@eturkes.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7447-1476"))
Description: Classifies missing protein intensities separately within
    experimental conditions, preserving on/off patterns that pooling can hide.
    Intensity cutoffs and a strict majority rule label feature-condition blocks
    likely missing-not-at-random (MNAR), likely missing-at-random (MAR), complete,
    insufficient, or absent. Inputs are unnormalised log2 proteomics intensities
    in ordinary matrices or SummarizedExperiment objects. Results include
    filtered data, classifications, cutoffs, optional rescue values, original
    observation counts, and feature drop reasons.
